Vendored files (verbatim, with include-only modifications)
----------------------------------------------------------
The following files were copied from scrcpy v5.0.1 and MODIFIED only to
decouple them from scrcpy's internal include layer so they compile standalone
against libavcodec / libavutil. The merge algorithm is unchanged. This
statement of changes is provided per Apache License 2.0, section 4.

  vendor/packet_merger.h
    Upstream: scrcpy v5.0.1, app/src/packet_merger.h
    Change:   replaced the scrcpy-internal include "common.h" with <stddef.h>.

  vendor/packet_merger.c
    Upstream: scrcpy v5.0.1, app/src/packet_merger.c
    Change:   replaced the scrcpy-internal include "util/log.h" with a minimal
              local LOG_OOM() macro (writes to stderr).

Reimplemented from reference (NOT vendored verbatim)
----------------------------------------------------
fb_decoder.h (and its implementation fb_decoder.c, added in a later milestone)
are FluxBridge-original code. They REIMPLEMENT the decode sequence proven by
scrcpy, citing as reference:

  scrcpy v5.0.1, app/src/decoder.c (sc_decoder_process_packet):
    avcodec_send_packet followed by a loop of avcodec_receive_frame, with
    AV_CODEC_FLAG_LOW_DELAY set on the codec context.
  scrcpy v5.0.1, app/src/demuxer.c:
    the 12-byte frame-header framing (pts/flags + payload length) and the
    AVCodecParameters setup (codec id + dimensions).

No scrcpy source beyond packet_merger.{c,h} is copied into FluxBridge; the rest
of scrcpy's decode path (hardware-decode selection, the frame-source /
packet-sink traits, the vecdeque and thread utilities, the stream session, and
scrcpy's logging) is intentionally not vendored.
